    {
      "name": "Work links",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Paste a work link (in the flow)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"{{youtubeUrl}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/conversation/message",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "conversation",
                "message"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Send this when the conversation is sitting on \"Enter your work link\" (92% on the Individual Author/Composer path).\n\nThe reply is plain chat messages, not a structured payload: describeSong() (workLinkGate.js) builds a card from Song / Artist / Film-Album / Released lines pulled straight from the provider response, then asks \"Is this your song?\". Artist is the flat credited-artist list from the source (Spotify artists[], or Gemini-parsed names from a YouTube title) - it does not say who composed vs sang vs wrote."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Confirm the song",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Yes, that's my song\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/conversation/message",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "conversation",
                "message"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Answers the confirmation card. matchCredits() (workMatch.service.js) compares the credited names against this member's AccountName/AccountAlias (trusted) and any names given earlier at this step (claimed), returning { matched, trust }.\n\n  matched  - a trusted or claimed name lines up with a credit -> saved, CreatedBy: chat:name-matched.\n  no match - describeCredits() asks which name(s) they are credited under (comma-separated, up to MAX_ALIAS_ATTEMPTS); still no match after that -> saved anyway so the member is never stuck, CreatedBy: chat:name-unverified.\n\nAuthor_Composer / Author_Lyricist are never written by this step - they stay null for staff (see AGENTS.md 'GROUNDED DATA ONLY')."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Spotify metadata (direct, legacy)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"url\": \"{{spotifyTrackUrl}}\",\n  \"actualName\": \"Pritam\",\n  \"stageName\": \"Pritam\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/spotify/metadata",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "spotify",
                "metadata"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The separate, legacy REST path for a Spotify claim (modules/spotify/), independent of the chat work-link step above. Writes an App_Accounts_WorkRegistration row only when { actualName, stageName } matches a credited artist on the track - a non-matching claim returns status: false and writes nothing."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No auth. Returns db up/down plus latencyMs - a first call over ~2s after an idle gap is the signature of AUTO_CLOSE being on."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "External - Spotify",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Get token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://accounts.spotify.com/api/token",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "accounts",
                "spotify",
                "com"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Client-credentials token, valid one hour. The Test script saves it into {{spotifyToken}} so the requests below just work. Fill {{spotifyClientId}} and {{spotifyClientSecret}} from .env first.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "{{spotifyClientId}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "{{spotifyClientSecret}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "client_credentials"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('spotifyToken', pm.response.json().access_token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Track",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{spotifyToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://api.spotify.com/v1/tracks/6VBhH7CyP56BXjp8VsDFPZ",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "api",
                "spotify",
                "com"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "tracks",
                "6VBhH7CyP56BXjp8VsDFPZ"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Kesariya. Look at artists[]: Pritam (composer), Arijit Singh (singer) and Amitabh Bhattacharya (lyricist) sit side by side with nothing marking which is which - the field only says who is credited, not who did what. That is why the backend's work-link match only ever asks \"is this member named in the credits\", never \"in what role\".\n\nCarries external_ids.isrc. Does NOT carry copyrights."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Album (copyrights)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{spotifyToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://api.spotify.com/v1/albums/1HeX4SmCFW4EPHQDvHgrVS",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "api",
                "spotify",
                "com"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "albums",
                "1HeX4SmCFW4EPHQDvHgrVS"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A separate call, because copyrights live on the album and not the track. The (P) line is the sound-recording label (Sony Music Entertainment India) - NOT the music publisher, which is a legally different entity. There is no `label` field in the response at all."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Search",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{spotifyToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://api.spotify.com/v1/search?q=Kesariya%20Brahmastra&type=track&limit=1",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "api",
                "spotify",
                "com"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "search"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "q",
                  "value": "Kesariya Brahmastra"
                },
                {
                  "key": "type",
                  "value": "track"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "1"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Find a track id to paste into the requests above."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "External - YouTube",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "videos.list (snippet)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://www.googleapis.com/youtube/v3/videos?part=snippet&id={{youtubeVideoId}}&key={{youtubeApiKey}}",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "www",
                "googleapis",
                "com"
              ],
              "path": [
                "youtube",
                "v3",
                "videos"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "part",
                  "value": "snippet"
                },
                {
                  "key": "id",
                  "value": "{{youtubeVideoId}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "key",
                  "value": "{{youtubeApiKey}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "The only reachable source of role-labelled credits: snippet.description carries \"Music - Pritam / Lyrics - Amitabh Bhattacharya / Singer - Arijit Singh\" on official label channels.\n\nAlso gives publishedAt (where YouTube ReleaseYear now comes from - it used to be null) and categoryId, where \"10\" means Music.\n\nFree: no billing account needed, 10,000 units/day, and this call costs 1 unit."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "oEmbed (keyless fallback)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://www.youtube.com/oembed?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fwatch%3Fv%3DBddP6PYo2gs&format=json",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "www",
                "youtube",
                "com"
              ],
              "path": [
                "oembed"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "url",
                  "value": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BddP6PYo2gs"
                },
                {
                  "key": "format",
                  "value": "json"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "What the backend (youtube.service.js) actually calls for every YouTube link - there is no YouTube Data API key configured for this project. Title, channel name and a thumbnail - no description, no publish date, so Gemini (gemini.service.js parseVideoTitle) works off the title text alone."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "External - Gemini",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Title parse",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"contents\": [\n    {\n      \"parts\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"You are given ONLY a YouTube video title and channel name. Split them into the fields below. Copy text that is present in the input; use null when a field is not present. Never add knowledge from outside the input - do not recall the song, guess a release year, or name people the input does not name. Set isMusicVideo to false when the input is not a song (a lecture, vlog, trailer, podcast). Return JSON: {\\\"isMusicVideo\\\": boolean, \\\"songName\\\": string|null, \\\"artists\\\": string[], \\\"filmOrAlbum\\\": string|null}\\n\\nTITLE: Kesariya - Brahmastra | Arijit Singh | Pritam | Amitabh B\\nCHANNEL: Sony Music India\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"generationConfig\": {\n    \"responseMimeType\": \"application/json\",\n    \"temperature\": 0\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{{geminiModel}}:generateContent?key={{geminiApiKey}}",
              "protocol": "https",
              "host": [
                "generativelanguage",
                "googleapis",
                "com"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1beta",
                "models",
                "{{geminiModel}}:generateContent"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "key",
                  "value": "{{geminiApiKey}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "The prompt the backend (gemini.service.js parseVideoTitle) uses to split a YouTube video title into song / artists / film-album. It is sent TEXT only - the oEmbed title and channel name, never the video itself - and forbidden from using outside knowledge.\n\nTo prove it does not invent: give it a title with no song info at all, e.g. \"My Vlog Day 3\" / CHANNEL: Random Creator. It should come back { \"isMusicVideo\": false, \"songName\": null, \"artists\": [], \"filmOrAlbum\": null } rather than guessing. Optional by design: with GEMINI_API_KEY blank, resolveWorkLink() falls back to the raw oEmbed title instead of calling this at all."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
